the original rin-tin-tin  was born on a battlefield in France in  1918 in the middle of World War one he  was found as a few day old puppy by a  young American GI named Lee Duncan who  had grown up living a very lonely life  and finding the truest companionship and  affection that he did ever find with  dogs  so in the middle of the war and this was  in the really brutal moment in the war  for him to find a litter of newborn  puppies struck him as nothing short of  miraculous and he felt that his whole  life changed at that very moment and in  fact it did Lee loved saying there will  always be a rin-tin-tin  and there was something about the way he  conducted his life that made it clear  that he believed that there was  something immortal about the dog and  what's interesting is that here we are  nearly a hundred years later still  talking about rin-ten-ten which to me  suggests that Lee was right that even  though this was partly a crazy notion  that a dog could live forever in fact he  has lived forever and the idea of that  pure hero dog has indeed lived forever  and I think we can assume it always will  he was both stronger and faster and  better and smarter but he was also  perfectly willing to chase a ball with  you and to snuggle up with you at the  end of a day so he was an unusual kind  of superhero a lot of what compelled me  to write the book was suddenly real  even though I thought rin-tin-tin was  merely a 50s television character I  discovered and was complete news to me  that he had had a just as illustrious  career or perhaps even more illustrious  career in silent film he made 27 silent  films they were shown all over the world  and that fact alone was astonishing to  me and it made me realize that very  likely my grandparents who were born in  Hungary and lived there until their 20s  had probably seen rin-tin-tin films when  they were growing up and the idea that  this figure could cut through  generations and worlds fascinated me and  it made me really want to write the the  story of that journey however you define  what it means to be an actor this dog  was it in addition to that though he had  something else which was that ability to  project an emotion that completely  enchanted people and made them fall in  love with him and that is what being a  star is I think so enjoy the movie and  thanks again for coming tonight
 

